-> **Limited Use.** The TDS extension's use of the data it reads follows the Chrome Web Store User Data Policy, including the Limited Use requirements. The TDS extension reads the text in the chat box on claude.ai, chatgpt.com and gemini.google.com to mask personal data before you send. On claude.ai only, and only if you switch restore on, it also reads the answers shown, to show the real values again on your screen. All of it happens on your device. The TDS extension's code makes no network calls, so it never sends this data to us or to anyone else. There are two ways to restore. With "Show real values in TDS's own panel" on, the real values are shown in a panel that the site's scripts cannot read. With "Put real values into the page itself" on, the real values go back into the site's page. The site's own scripts can read them on your screen, and could send them back to the site (for example through analytics or error reports). Other browser extensions that can read the page can see them too. Both are off by default; you choose whether to switch one on. It is not sold, not used for advertising, not used to decide creditworthiness, and not read by people. The only data we receive is a bug report that you choose to e-mail us yourself.
+> **Limited Use.** The TDS extension's use of the data it reads follows the Chrome Web Store User Data Policy, including the Limited Use requirements. The TDS extension reads the text in the chat box on claude.ai, chatgpt.com and gemini.google.com to mask personal data before you send. On claude.ai only, and only if you switch restore on, it also reads the answers shown, to show the real values again on your screen. All of it happens on your device. The TDS extension's code makes no network calls, so it never sends this data to us or to anyone else. There are two ways to restore. With "Show real values in TDS's own panel" on, the real values are shown in a panel that the site's own scripts cannot read. Other browser extensions that can read the page may still be able to read it, and anything on your screen can be seen in screen sharing or a screenshot. With "Put real values into the page itself" on, the real values go back into the site's page. The site's own scripts can read them on your screen, and could send them back to the site (for example through analytics or error reports). Other browser extensions that can read the page can see them too. Both are off by default; you choose whether to switch one on. It is not sold, not used for advertising, not used to decide creditworthiness, and not read by people. The only data we receive is a bug report that you choose to e-mail us yourself.
